# The Bare toolchain (bare-build, bare-pack) resolves modules itself rather than
# deferring to Node, and it will not follow pnpm's symlinks into .pnpm. Transitive
# dependencies are therefore invisible to it and a build fails with
# MODULE_NOT_FOUND on things like bare-abort.
#
# Hoisting makes every dependency a real directory under the workspace root, which
# is the layout that resolver expects.
#
# The related trap: bare-build must also be invoked FROM the workspace root, so
# node_modules is inside its base directory. Run from apps/supervisor it builds a
# binary that crashes at startup looking for
# file:///C:/node_modules/bare-worker/lib/worker-thread.js. See scripts/make.mjs.
node-linker=hoisted
